    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `GET /api/owners/{id}` response DTO (`OwnerDto`) is generated from `openapi.yml` and populated by `OwnerMapper`, so I made two coordinated edits:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` property to the `Owner` schema with an `enum` of `EMAIL`/`PHONE`. This generates a `OwnerDto.ContactPreferenceEnum` type at build time.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` that computes the value: `EMAIL` when `owner.getEmail()` is non-null and non-blank, otherwise `PHONE`.\n\nBoth new acceptance tests pass:\n- `corePhoneWhenNoEmail` \u2192 `contactPreference` = `PHONE` when no email\n- `functionalityEmailWhenPresent` \u2192 `contactPreference` = `EMAIL` when an email is present\n\nThis follows the existing pattern in the codebase (e.g. `membershipLevel`, `locality`) which likewise derive fields via the mapper rather than through OfficeFloor function steps, since the derivation is a pure mapping over the entity.",
